1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,223
DAW in DAW: a complete multitrack digital audio workstation, written in pure Lua, running

2
00:00:06,223 --> 00:00:07,139
inside REAPER.

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:09,718
Think Neovim inside Neovim.

4
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:14,920
REAPER supplies the host primitives: the audio engine, MIDI, undo, rendering and the save

5
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,329
format.

6
00:00:15,329 --> 00:00:20,472
This project supplies the whole application on top: its own arrangement view, piano roll

7
00:00:20,472 --> 00:00:25,557
mixer, effects rack and export dialog, all drawn with REAPER's built in graphics A P I.

8
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,933
There is no second model and no second audio engine.

9
00:00:29,933 --> 00:00:35,772
Every track, clip, note, fader and effect is a REAPER object, so the same project opens in

10
00:00:35,772 --> 00:00:40,119
REAPER's normal interface as ordinary tracks, items and F X chains.

11
00:00:40,119 --> 00:00:42,973
Edits from either side show up in the other.

12
00:00:42,973 --> 00:00:45,308
Every edit is one native undo point.

13
00:00:46,310 --> 00:00:54,527
It is 3,597 lines of Lua in 22 files, with no dependencies beyond ReaScript and gfx.

14
00:00:54,527 --> 00:00:58,049
Copy the folder and run daw dot lua.

15
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:05,020
The repo's generated test report shows 598 automated checks across 11 suites, with 0 failures.

16
00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:10,545
354 are pure Lua unit tests that need no REAPER, and the rest run inside a real REAPER.

17
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:14,068
Performance is measured, not assumed.

18
00:01:14,068 --> 00:01:19,875
With 16 tracks, 102 clips and 1,000 notes, user interface work per frame averages 1.5

19
00:01:19,875 --> 00:01:26,229
milliseconds idle, 2.3 while dragging a clip, and 3.7 during playback, against a thirty three

20
00:01:26,229 --> 00:01:27,528
millisecond budget.

21
00:01:28,530 --> 00:01:29,502
The honest status.

22
00:01:29,502 --> 00:01:33,766
It is tested on macOS with REAPER seven point three nine on Apple Silicon only.

23
00:01:33,766 --> 00:01:38,732
The tests that post real operating system mouse and keyboard events were written, but need a

24
00:01:38,732 --> 00:01:43,105
macOS permission that was not available, so they have not been run to completion.

25
00:01:43,105 --> 00:01:46,776
The app's real frame loop is exercised with synthetic input instead.

26
00:01:46,776 --> 00:01:50,230
There is one tempo, no automation lanes, and no audio recording.

27
00:01:51,230 --> 00:01:57,332
Clone the repo, run run dot s h with the example song, and listen to what it made.

